<title>UK: GOLF-WOODS REGAINS TOP SPOT IN WORLD RANKINGS.</title>
<headline>GOLF-WOODS REGAINS TOP SPOT IN WORLD RANKINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tiger Woods regained top spot from</p>
<p>Greg Norman in the world rankings issued Monday following his</p>
<p>victory in the Western Open in Lemont, Illinois at the weekend.</p>
<p>Scotland's Colin Montgomerie, winner of the Irish Open,</p>
<p>retains fourth place behind Ernie Els of South Africa.</p>
<p>Leaders:</p>
<p>  1. Tiger Woods (U.S.)	    10.71 points average</p>
<p>  2. Greg Norman (Australia)     10.38</p>
<p>  3. Ernie Els (South Africa)    10.24</p>
<p>  4. Colin Montgomerie (Britain)  9.75</p>
<p>  5. Nick Price (Zimbabwe)	  9.57</p>
<p>  6. Tom Lehman (U.S.)		8.75</p>
<p>  7. Steve Elkington (Australia)  8.60</p>
<p>  8. Masashi Ozaki (Japan)	  7.93</p>
<p>  9. Mark O'Meara (U.S.)	    7.61</p>
<p> 10. Nick Faldo (Britain)	   7.27</p>
<p> 11. Phil Mickelson (U.S.)	  7.18</p>
<p> 12. Scott Hoch (U.S.)		6.85</p>
<p> 13. Brad Faxon (U.S.)		6.80</p>
<p> 14. Fred Couples (U.S.)	    6.74</p>
<p> 15. Jesper Parnevik (Sweden)     5.67</p>
<p> 16. Ian Woosnam (Britain)	  5.59</p>
<p> 17. Davis Love III (U.S.)	  5.43</p>
<p> 18. Bernhard Langer (Germany)    5.22</p>
<p> 19. Justin Leonard (U.S.)	  5.12</p>
<p> 20. Tom Watson (U.S.)		5.10</p>
